# Experiment protocol: <name>

*A checklist, not a copy-form: structure is free, but every field occurs —
if need be as "n/a — <why>". `protocol-check` enforces this.*

- **One question per protocol.** A throwaway test with no kept number needs
  none — neither does an exploration notebook (→ §2.D7).
- **One field = one line.** If the justification needs more room, it goes
  into a note; the [[wikilink]] stays here.
- **The form is cut by tier** (`lib exp --cost seconds` stamps the `seconds` cut:
  head · question · criterion · admissibility · terms · data · unit ·
  exclusions · result; with `--model` also model · prompt · null condition;
  the full form adds the rest; `--report` the † fields). One template, three
  cuts — a field the cut left out is not owed (→ §2.A14).
- **† = report field.** Due once `frozen = true` in the head — those in
  Summary and Result once a run is written back as well; leave the
  placeholder until then (`lib exp <name> --report` appends them).
- **`[C…]`/`[A…]`/`[B…]` = intent ids**, one per promise to the code:
  **C** criterion — which value of which metric supports the hypothesis,
  one per conjunct · **A** admissibility — an outcome-neutral check that
  must pass in the same run before any C verdict is issued (yield,
  coverage, control, anchor) · **B** branch — what a result licenses next.
  C judges, A releases the judgement, B says what follows. Each id
  reappears as a lowercase key in the reportable run's metrics.json
  (`c1_pass`, `a1_pass`, `b1_branch`); `intent-check` compares the two sets
  (→ §2.A1a). To bind constants and code too, add the same promises as
  `[[promise]]` tables to the ```toml block below (labkit
  `docs/promise-block.md`).
- **`→ §2.x`** = the rule of that number in `docs/arbeitsstandard.md`; the
  reasoning, the evidence and the term legend live there — here only what
  the field demands.

```toml
[protocol]
standard = "0.18"
id = "<protocol-id>"        # stamped by `lib exp`, never typed
type = "<exploratory | confirmatory>"
# exploratory: generates hypotheses, none of it reported as a test;
# confirmatory: tests a hypothesis fixed before the run
cost = "<seconds | minutes | hours>"
# the price of a REPEAT, not whether a model is involved — seconds:
# rerunnable at will, incl. a handful of model calls for a minute and cents;
# minutes: a model pass you would not casually redo; hours: expensive or
# irreversible (→ §2.A14)
frozen = false              # true only after the instrument check
preflight_audit = ""
# date · scope sha · N findings (blockers fixed / accepted with reason /
# dismissed with reason) — the code-vs-intent audit after the instrument
# check, before freezing (→ §2.A12)
```

*Field labels English; content in German or English. Explanations,
examples, rationale for each field: `protocol-field-guide.md`
(`protocol-check --guide` prints the path; thesis repos:
`templates/PROTOCOL-FIELD-GUIDE.md`). A run of seconds takes the
seconds cut (`lib exp <name> --cost seconds`, `--model <alias>` with a model in the loop).*

